# ── Derived RBAC oracles: NEVER textually merged ───────────────────────────────
# These three fixtures are generated by `php artisan rbac:derive-access` against a
# synced DB. Git's textual auto-merge of two independently regenerated fixtures
# succeeds and produces a file that is wrong AND green — it happened once already
# (a duplicated route-access-map entry via a rebase). -merge forces a conflict, and
# the ONLY correct resolution to that conflict is to regenerate against the merged
# HEAD, per RBAC implementation plan §4.2. Never resolve one of these by hand.
#
# Only these three. The other committed baselines (authz/boundary/money/
# runtime-zero/identifier lint, phpstan, tsc, tests/ratchet-baseline.txt) are
# SET-like and shrink-enforced by their gates, so a union auto-merge is
# semantically what both branches wanted and the next gate run catches any
# divergence. These three are whole-tree SNAPSHOTS of the route surface — a
# union of two regenerations is a snapshot of neither tree, and nothing
# re-derives it. That asymmetry is why the guard is narrow.
tests/fixtures/route-access-map.json          -merge
tests/fixtures/rbac-grants-baseline.json      -merge
tests/fixtures/route-middleware-baseline.json -merge
